hadiths[28]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17824","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hariz ibn 'Uthman, he said: We were young boys sitting with Abdullah ibn Busr, and he was among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we did not know how to ask him well, so I said: Was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) an old man? He said: There were white hairs in his tuft beneath the lower lip."
"17825","Hushaym narrated to us: Hisham ibn Yusuf informed us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Busr narrating that his father prepared food for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and invited him, and he accepted. Then when he finished his food, he said: O Allah, forgive them and have mercy upon them and bless for them in what You have provided them."
"17826","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zahiriyyah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Busr, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was addressing the people on Friday and said: Sit, for you have harmed and delayed."
"17827","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Abdullah ibn Busr, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted, and they mentioned a waterskin and food and drink, and he would eat dates and place the stones upon the backs of his two fingers, then throw them. Then he stood and mounted a white mule of his, and I took its bridle and said: O Prophet of Allah, supplicate to Allah for us. He said: O Allah, bless for them in what You have provided them, and forgive them and have mercy upon them."
"17828","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Ibn Abdullah ibn Busr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, and my grandmother presented to him dates he was eating sparingly, and cooked for him, and we gave them drink, and the cup was used up, so I brought another cup, and I was the servant. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give the cup to the one at whom it had ended."
"17829","'Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us: Al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Busr narrated to me, he said: My sister would sometimes send me with something to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a gift to him, and he would accept it from me."
"17830","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Safwan ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Busr al-Mazini narrated to me, he said: My father sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inviting him to food, so he came with me. When I neared the house I hastened and informed my parents, so they came out and met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and welcomed him, and we placed for him a mantle that was with us, shaggy. He sat upon it. Then my father said to my mother: Bring your food. She brought a bowl in which was flour she had kneaded with water and salt, and placed it before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Take in the name of Allah from around it, and leave its top, for indeed the blessing is in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate, and we ate with him, and some remainder remained of it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive them and have mercy upon them and bless upon them and widen for them in their provisions."
"17831","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Safwan narrated to us: Azhar ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Busr, he said: I heard a hadith long ago: If you are among a people of twenty men or less or more, and you look over their faces and do not see among them a man who is feared for the sake of Allah, then know that the matter has become weak."
"17832","Ali ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us: Hassan ibn Nuh narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Busr, he said: Two Bedouins came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said: Who are the best of men, O Muhammad? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He whose life is long and whose deed is good. And the other said: The laws of Islam have become many for us, so a comprehensive door that we may hold to. He said: Your tongue shall remain moist with the remembrance of Allah Almighty."
"17833","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Hariz narrated to us, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Busr al-Mazini, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: Did you see the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was he an old man? He said: There were white hairs in his tuft beneath the lower lip."
"17834","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Hariz narrated to us, he said: I said to Abdullah ibn Busr, while we were young boys not comprehending knowledge: Was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) an old man? He said: There were white hairs in his tuft beneath the lower lip."
"17835","'Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Abdullah ibn Busr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to my father and alighted with him, or my father said to him: Alight with me. He said: He brought him food and hays and sawiq, and he ate it, and he would eat dates and cast the stones, describing with his two fingers the forefinger and the middle with their backs from his mouth. Then he brought him drink and he drank, then he passed it to the one on his right. Then he stood and he took the bridle of his mount and said: Supplicate to Allah Almighty for me. He said: O Allah, bless for them in what You have provided them, and forgive them and have mercy upon them."
"17836","Bahz narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Khumayr informed me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Busr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted with my father, or my father said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Alight with me. He said: He alighted with him, and he brought him food or hays. He said: He ate. Then he brought him drink. He said: He drank. He said: Then he passed to the one on his right. He said: And when he ate he would cast the stone, and Shu'bah described that he placed the stone upon the forefinger and the middle, then threw it. His father said to him: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate for us. He said: O Allah, bless for them in what You have provided them, and forgive them and have mercy upon them."
"17837","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, meaning Ibn Jabir, narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad, from the two sons of Busr al-Sulamiyyayn, he said: I entered upon them and said: May Allah have mercy upon you, a man among us rides his mount and strikes it with the whip and pulls it with the bridle; have you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning that? They said: No, we did not hear anything from him concerning that. Then a woman called from inside the house: O questioner, indeed Allah Almighty says: And there is no creature on earth nor a bird flying with its wings except communities like you; We did not neglect in the Book anything. They said: This is our sister, and she is older than us, and she met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17838","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Talaqani narrated to us, he said: Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Hassan, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Busr al-Mazini say: You see this hand of mine; I pledged with it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast Saturday except in what has been obligated upon you."
"17839","Hisham ibn Sa'id Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Busr, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me, he said: My sister would send me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a gift, and he would accept it."
"17840","Hisham ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Busr narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would accept the gift and would not accept charity."
"17841","'Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abu Abdullah al-Hasan ibn Ayyub al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Busr showed me a mole on his forehead, so I placed my finger upon it, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his finger upon it, then said: You shall live to reach a horn [old age]. Abu Abdullah said: And he had abundant hair."
"17842","Ali ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Nuh, a Himsi, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Busr say: You see this palm of mine; I bear witness that I placed it upon the palm of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And he forbade fasting Saturday except in an obligation, and said: If one of you finds nothing except grapevine bark, let him break his fast upon it."
"17843","Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us: Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ibn Abi Bilal, from Abdullah ibn Busr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between the great battle and the conquest of the city are six years, and the false Messiah, the Dajjal, will emerge in the seventh."
"17844","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from al-Hakam: Isma'il, meaning Ibn 'Ayyash, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsibi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Busr al-Mazini, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to a people's house, would come to it from the side of its wall and would not come to it facing its door."
"17845","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Khumayr al-Rahabi narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Busr al-Mazini, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is none of my nation of anyone except that I shall know him on the Day of Resurrection. They said: And how will you know them, O Messenger of Allah, among the multitude of creatures? He said: What do you think, if you entered an enclosure in which were dark black horses, and in it a horse blaze-faced and white-footed, would you not recognize it from them? He said: Yes. He said: Then indeed my nation on that day are radiant from prostration, white-fore-armed from ablution."
"17846","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from al-Hakam, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsibi narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Busr, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to a door seeking permission, would not face it; he says: He would walk along the wall until he sought permission, then permission would be given to him or he would leave."
"17847","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Abdullah ibn Busr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted with my father. He said: We brought him food and a waterskin, and he ate from it. Then dates were brought, and he would eat them and cast the stones with his two fingers, joining the forefinger and the middle. Shu'bah said: It is my conjecture, and it is in it, Allah willing. Then drink was brought, and he drank it, then passed it to the one on his right. He said: My father said, taking the bridle of his mount: Supplicate to Allah for us. He said: O Allah, bless for them in what You have provided them, and forgive them and have mercy upon them."
"17848","Rawh narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Busr narrating from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited them, and he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Ibn Ja'far."
"17849","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Busr on Friday, and a man came stepping over the necks of the people while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was addressing, and he said: Sit, for you have harmed and delayed."
"17850","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, from 'Amr ibn Qays, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Busr say: Two Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are best? He said: He whose life is long and whose deed is good. And the other said: O Messenger of Allah, the laws of Islam have become many for me, so command me with a matter I may hold fast to. He said: Your tongue shall remain moist with the remembrance of Allah Almighty."
"17851","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Hariz ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Busr, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) an old man? He said: He was younger than that, but there were white hairs in his beard, and perhaps he said: In his tuft beneath the lower lip."
